caption: TWELVE MAINTAINED GATES: CURRENT ROSTER
campaign-component: twelve-maintained-gates-current-roster

The twelve maintained Gates form seven major fronts. Their motives are deliberately different: conquest, military expansion, colonial nesting, defensive occupation, refugee colonization, invasive ecology, and animal migration.

Gates 1–3: The Waaagh

Source: Undeveloped Warhammer 40,000-inspired dimension.

Status: Concept accepted; exact Orks undeveloped.

LOCKED: The Orks do not come from Stellar Conflict.

LOCKED: Three connected Gates support one Waaagh front.

LOCKED: The Waaagh is aggressive, expansionist, destructive, and interested in fighting, looting, industrial systems, vehicles, and weapons.

OPEN: Develop the 40k-inspired dimension, GATES Orks, Waaagh command structure, troop composition, technology, psychic Gate maintenance, and exact objectives.

REFERENCE: A development placeholder exists in Dimensions/Warhammer 40,000-Inspired Dimension.

Gates 4–5: The Scorge Undead Offensive

Source: The Scorge, from Eternal War.

Status: Source accepted; specifics undeveloped.

LOCKED: The mass undead army does not originate in Dragon’s Roost.

LOCKED: The Scorge conducts a coordinated military invasion through two Gates.

LOCKED: This is an organized army rather than a spontaneous undead outbreak.

PROVISIONAL: One Gate serves as the vanguard and territorial-seizure front; the other delivers heavy forces, necromancers, command staff, siege assets, and Gate-maintenance infrastructure.

PROVISIONAL: Local corpses can be recruited only through deliberate Scorge necromancy, marking, processing, or ritual, rather than rising automatically.

OPEN: Develop Scorge force composition, command hierarchy, military objective, Gate anchors, local corpse conversion, and relationship to the wider Eternal War.

Gates 6–7: Bugworld Psionic Colony

Source: Bugworld.

Status: Core concept accepted; development required.

LOCKED: Bugworld maintains its Gates psionically.

LOCKED: Maintenance is distributed across a psychic network rather than resting on one obvious caster.

PROVISIONAL: One Gate functions as a harvest and combat front in a dense district; the other functions as a brood, nesting, and infrastructure front in terrain suitable for subterranean expansion.

PROVISIONAL: Major brain organisms each contribute to Gate stability. Destroying or disrupting them progressively weakens both Gates.

OPEN: Define the psychic hierarchy, hive structure, breeding rate, biomass needs, adaptive biology, ability to incorporate local traits, and whether the swarm can negotiate.

Gates 8–9: ADhN Defensive Enclave

Source: ADhN.

Status: Core behavior accepted.

LOCKED: ADhN is ultimately friendly.

LOCKED: ADhN has suffered heavily from Steelhaven and is deeply distrustful of humans.

LOCKED: ADhN forces are defensive rather than expansionist.

LOCKED: They do not fire first.

LOCKED: They establish clear security lines and warnings around the Gates.

LOCKED: Anyone who knowingly crosses the final line or attacks their position may be killed immediately and decisively.

LOCKED: Their goals are to secure the Gates, prevent hostile entry into ADhN, recover displaced machines, determine whether the event is a Steelhaven attack, and establish contact with a trustworthy authority.

PROVISIONAL: They construct technological stabilization pylons that maintain the Gates.

PROVISIONAL: They may recognize the meerkat robots as persons or potential intelligences, providing an early diplomatic opening.

OPEN: Define contact protocols, perimeter size, force composition, proof sufficient to distinguish Furui Tokyo from Steelhaven, and conditions for negotiated withdrawal or controlled border access.

Gate 10: Yao Territorial Exodus

Source: The Land of Lakes and Rivers/Wuxia.

Status: Core motive accepted.

LOCKED: The Yao are trying to leave Wuxia and escape the Celestial Court.

LOCKED: They intend to claim territory on the far side and therefore constitute an invasion even when many participants are refugees or settlers.

LOCKED: The Wuxia time differential gives the Yao months of subjective preparation before the party arrives.

LOCKED: The force includes more than warriors: families, dependents, craftspeople, ritualists, supplies, political factions, and possibly ordinary Wuxia people escaping with them.

LOCKED: They establish a New Yao Court or equivalent territorial authority in Furui Tokyo.

LOCKED: Some factions may prefer negotiated settlement; others regard local humans as weak subjects, prey, or obstacles.

OPEN: Define leadership, population, major factions, claimed territory, Celestial Court response, ritual Gate maintenance, and acceptable settlement terms.

Gate 11: The Haneda Bloom

Source: Undeveloped Borderlands-inspired/flora-kaiju dimension.

Status: Core concept accepted; source setting undeveloped.

LOCKED: The Haneda Bloom is botanical and kaiju-scale rather than a Fleshworld incursion.

LOCKED: Weird flora-kaiju grow through and maintain the Gate.

LOCKED: The Gate is physically and supernaturally bridged by roots, rhizomes, vines, or another giant transdimensional plant structure.

LOCKED: The incursion rapidly converts Haneda Airport into an alien botanical ecosystem.

PROVISIONAL: Threats include tower-sized flowers, runway-breaking roots, mobile carnivorous plants, spore clouds, seed artillery, photosynthetic animal-like organisms, and adaptive fire-resistant growth.

PROVISIONAL: Bramble may have a communication or ecological solution unavailable to conventional military forces.

OPEN: Develop the flora-kaiju dimension, the central organism, plant intelligence, growth rate, ecological motives, Gate-maintenance mechanism, and nonviolent withdrawal conditions.

OPEN: Fleshworld is under reconsideration and may eventually be retired or merged, but should not yet be deleted.

Gate 12: The Brood Passage

Source: Megaworld.

Status: Core concept accepted; ecology undeveloped.

LOCKED: The Brood Passage is distinct from the Haneda Bloom.

LOCKED: Megaworld supplies animalistic kaiju migration, nesting, parasites, scavengers, and symbiotic species.

LOCKED: The Gate opens in Tokyo Bay so large creatures can emerge without immediately becoming trapped among buildings.

LOCKED: The creatures are not a political invasion force. They interpret Tokyo Bay as new nesting, feeding, or migration territory.

LOCKED: A brood mother, territorial adult, or similarly powerful creature maintains the Gate through supernatural vitality or instinct.

OPEN: Develop the brood species, guardian and juvenile sizes, parasites, nesting behavior, motivation, military response, and ways to redirect the migration without extermination.
